WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.009
Jenna Ortega will not be returning for "Scream
VII".

00:00:04.009 --> 00:00:08.611
If it doesn't have anything to do with the
Melissa Barrera drama, then what's going on?

00:00:08.611 --> 00:00:11.276
And what does it mean for the fate of the
movie?

00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:15.799
Earlier this week, it was reported that Melissa
Barrera would not be returning for the currently

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:17.859
untitled seventh "Scream" film.

00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:23.740
Barrera, who plays Sam Carpenter in the franchise,
was fired by Spyglass Media over social media

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.720
posts relating to the ongoing Israeli-Palestinian
conflict.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.440
"Being famous isn't all it's cracked up to
be."

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:36.230
Barrera's dismissal from the highly-anticipated
"Scream VII" has proven to be controversial,

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.550
and left fans of the long-running slasher
series uneasy about the franchise's future.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:46.000
Now, Deadline reports that Ortega, who stars
as Tara Carpenter, will also not be returning

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.350
to reprise her role.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.940
The outlet notes that Ortega, who has emerged
as one of Hollywood's most in-demand talents

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:57.720
since her 2022 "Scream" debut, is leaving
the franchise to film "Wednesday" Season 2.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.319
Ortega's decision reportedly has nothing to
do with Barrera's firing.

00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:06.100
Her choice to call it curtains on "Scream"
was made months ago, according to The Hollywood

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.808
Reporter, though it hasn't escaped many that
the bombshell news comes in the wake of yesterday's controversial move.

00:01:11.808 --> 00:01:14.087
"Scream 7" is still in early production.

00:01:14.087 --> 00:01:20.340
In fact, Deadline says a script isn't even
ready yet — and Ortega has big plans occupying her schedule.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.100
The "X" actress is heading to Ireland in April
to start filming "Wednesday" Season 2, and

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.240
needs to wrap up the decades-in-the-making
"Beetlejuice 2," which was forced to pause

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.810
production due to the 2023 SAG-AFTRA strike.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:37.555
With Ortega and Barrera out of the picture,
it's unclear what a "Scream 7" would look like.

00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:42.939
After all, the franchise made it pretty darn
clear with 2023's "Scream VI" that the Carpenter

00:01:42.939 --> 00:01:46.860
sisters would be at the heart of the series
going forward.

00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:49.068
"Sam?

00:01:49.068 --> 00:01:51.011
You coming?"

00:01:51.011 --> 00:01:55.060
It's sort of surprising that the "Scream"
franchise has found itself in this position

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.399
considering just how prominent the series
has been in recent years.

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:03.270
After remaining dormant for over a decade,
directors Matt Bettinelli-Olpin and Tyler

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:08.830
Gillett revived the slasher series with 2022's
"Scream," which saw the Carpenter sisters

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:13.730
teaming up with old guard Sidney Prescott
and Gale Weathers to protect the town of Woodsboro

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.190
from a new Ghostface.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:21.680
The film emerged as a substantial success,
grossing over $138 million worldwide and proving

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.959
that the series could be relevant to Gen Z.

00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:29.500
Paramount Pictures and Spyglass quickly produced
a sequel, releasing "Scream VI" to even greater

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.400
critical and financial acclaim earlier this
year.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.500
The "Scream" franchise hasn't even peaked
yet, but it seems as if its wings are being cut off.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.030
"Happy Death Day" series director Christopher
Landon was roped in earlier this year to direct

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.273
the upcoming "Scream VII," but it's unclear
when production on the seventh outing will start.

00:02:47.273 --> 00:02:50.640
For Ortega, however, this is a major strategic
move.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.890
The actress has turned into a superstar since
"Scream," and it makes sense that she wants

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.950
to double down on "Wednesday," the Netflix
series that turned her into an overnight horror

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.142
icon and an Emmy nominee.

00:03:01.142 --> 00:03:05.260
While the "Scream" franchise has always been
great to her, they were never really her projects

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.540
to begin with, unlike "Wednesday," which is
clearly a showcase for her talents as a lead star.

